## Why This Is Asked
Assesses end-to-end OTCA thinking: data model, on-ingest privacy, per-tenant residency, and a simple QoS rule at the edge.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA governance and per-tenant residency
- Ingest-time privacy: redaction and per-tenant hashing
- Latency-variance based event filtering
- Streaming path: Client -> Edge -> Regional Kafka -> Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions
- Test strategy: privacy, QoS, retention, and cross-region consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
function rollingMedian(nums) {
  if (!nums.length) return 0;
  const s = nums.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const m = Math.floor(s.length/2);
  return s.length%2 ? s[m] : (s[m-1]+s[m])/2;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt the latency rule for bursty traffic?
- How would you verify per-tenant salt security in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical schema evolution, privacy at ingest, and how it affects dashboards.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA streaming, schema evolution, privacy policies, per-tenant isolation
- Schema Registry, Avro/JSON schemas, backward compatibility
- Ingestion pipeline and storage layout (Parquet partitions)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy application at ingest
function applyPolicy(tenant, payload){
  const policy = getPolicy(tenant);
  if(policy.redact) redact(payload, policy.fields);
  if(policy.drop) dropFields(payload, policy.fields);
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you migrate existing data when a policy changes?
- How would you monitor schema compatibility over time?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable OTCA path with privacy-first constraints, multi-region residency, dynamic redaction, and compliant purge workflows.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant residency and data locality
- Dynamic, versioned redaction rules
- Immutable regional logs and global canonical events
- Canary rollouts and zero-downtime config reloads
- GDPR/CCPA purge and auditability

Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event, policy) {
  const out = { ...event };
  if (policy.redactPII && out.user?.email) delete out.user.email;
  if (policy.redactPhone && out.user?.phone) delete out.user.phone;
  return out;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate purge requests across regions with clock skew?
- Which metrics indicate redaction misfires under load and how would you triage them?
